; Regression test for issue #3356:
; getquote: an unreadable quote is an error with no context, and a batch
; then skips pclose()
;
; A getquote script that prints a line parse_price_directive() cannot read
; used to abort the whole report with a bare "No quantity specified for
; amount".  Now the line only costs a warning naming the commodity, the
; line and the error, the batch reads on, and the per-commodity fallback
; tries again; a bare word gets the same warning.  The prices the batch
; did read are still used: AAPL is valued at the quoted $150.00, not its
; old $100.00, so Brokerage totals $3000.00 rather than $2500.00.

2024/01/15 Buy Stock A
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL
    Assets:Checking        $-1000.00

2024/01/15 Buy Stock B
    Assets:Brokerage        10 BADLINE
    Assets:Checking        $-1000.00

2024/01/15 Buy Stock C
    Assets:Brokerage        10 BAREWORD
    Assets:Checking        $-500.00

test bal --market --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote.sh -> 0
            $3000.00  Assets
            $3000.00    Brokerage
           $-2500.00    Checking
--------------------
             $500.00
__ERROR__
Warning: Price quote script returned an unreadable price for commodity 'BADLINE': '2024/06/15 BADLINE N/A' (No quantity specified for amount)
Warning: Price quote script returned an unreadable price: 'N/A'
Warning: Price quote script returned an unreadable price for commodity 'BADLINE': '2024/06/15 BADLINE N/A' (No quantity specified for amount)
Warning: Price quote script returned an unreadable price for commodity 'BAREWORD': 'N/A'
end test
